## std/scrolls.pengu
## Operaciones sobre strings: consulta, búsqueda, corte, recorte, reemplazo,
## división, unión, alineación, clasificación ASCII, comparación y parseo.
##
## Cada operación existe dos veces: como método (`calling s.trim`) y como
## función de módulo (`calling scrolls.trim with s`), que delega en el método.
## `join` solo es función de módulo; `parse_int`/`parse_float`, solo métodos.
##
## ## Ownership
## Un `string` es un valor: nada muta `self`. El texto y los `list` devueltos
## son nuevos y auto-banishables; los parámetros nunca se banishean.
##
## ## ASCII y bytes
## El módulo es ASCII y trabaja a nivel de byte: `len`, los índices, `chars`,
## `bytes` y los cortes cuentan bytes, no puntos de código UTF-8; un carácter
## multi-byte se ve como varios bytes y `char_at` o `reverse` pueden partirlo.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## import std.scrolls
## import std.spark
##
## weave main into int:
##     var raw as string is "  Hello, World  "
##     var clean as string is calling raw.trim
##     var parts as list of string is calling clean.split with ", "
##     var joined as string is calling scrolls.join with parts, "|"
##     calling spark.println with joined
##     return 0
## ```
##
## ## Notas de diseño
## - **Sin `+` para strings** (E0005): la única composición es la interpolación
##   `"{expr}"`; `_concat` es el único punto de acumulación del módulo.
## - **`@deprecated` es una convención documental**: el toolchain no soporta
##   deprecación; los alias empiezan su docstring por `## @deprecated Use X`.
## - **Forma funcional.** Cada método tiene su `weave` de módulo, que solo
##   añade el receptor `s` y delega; su contrato es el del método ya
##   documentado arriba (no se repite la misma línea 68 veces).
## - **Tests internos sin `std.ward`** (`ward` importa `scrolls`, E0004): la
##   sección `# --- Tests ---` usa un harness privado sobre `spark.panic`.
## - **`compare`** devuelve -1/0/1 por el prefijo común y, si empata, la
##   longitud; `is_space` es false para "" (legado) e `is_blank` es true.
## - **`parse_int`** delega en `spark.parse_int` (acepta espacios, rechaza el
##   desbordamiento); **`parse_float`** calcula dígito a dígito y no acepta
##   exponentes. Ninguno tiene forma funcional: `insignia pengu_` los emitiría
##   como los intrínsecos `pengu_parse_int`/`pengu_parse_float`.
##
## ## Migración
##
## Los nombres antiguos siguen funcionando como alias que delegan.
##
## | Antiguo | Canónico |
## |---|---|
## | `calling s.to_lower` / `s.to_upper` | `calling s.lower` / `s.upper` |
## | `calling s.title_case` | `calling s.title` |
## | `calling s.find` / `s.rfind` | `calling s.index_of` / `s.last_index_of` |
## | `calling s.count_matches` | `calling s.count` |
## | `calling s.lstrip` / `s.rstrip` | `calling s.trim_start` / `calling s.trim_end` |
## | `calling s.is_whitespace` | `calling s.is_space` |
## | `calling s.pad_left` / `s.pad_right` | `calling s.rjust` / `calling s.ljust` |
##
## Nuevas: `words`, `lines`, `pascal_case`, `snake_case`, `kebab_case`,
## `is_blank`, `is_numeric`, `parse_int`, `parse_float`, `repeat_join`.

# --- Directivas de módulo ------------------------------------------------
insignia pengu_

# --- Imports ------------------------------------------------------------
import std.spark

# --- Enchantings --------------------------------------------------------
## Métodos de `string`: consulta, transformación, predicados y parseo.
enchanting string:
    # --- Longitud e iteración ------------------------------------------
    ## Número de bytes del string.
    weave len into int:
        let sv is essence of self
        return sv length
    ## True cuando el string está vacío (longitud 0).
    weave is_empty into bool:
        let sv is essence of self
        return sv length == 0
    ## Lista con cada byte como un string de un carácter.
    weave chars into list of string:
        let sv is essence of self
        let parts is for ch in sv then ch
        return parts
    ## Lista con el código numérico de cada byte.
    weave bytes into list of int:
        let sv is essence of self
        let codes is for ch in sv then ord ch
        return codes

    # --- Búsqueda -------------------------------------------------------
    ## True cuando `sub` aparece en alguna posición del string.
    weave contains with sub as string into bool:
        let sv is essence of self
        return (calling _index_of_from with sv, sub, 0) >= 0
    ## True cuando el string empieza por `prefix` (un `prefix` vacío encaja).
    weave starts_with with prefix as string into bool:
        let sv is essence of self
        return calling _has_prefix_at with sv, prefix, 0
    ## True cuando el string termina en `suffix` (un `suffix` vacío encaja).
    weave ends_with with suffix as string into bool:
        let sv is essence of self
        let sl as int is suffix length
        let ll as int is sv length
        if sl > ll:
            return false
        return calling _has_prefix_at with sv, suffix, ll - sl
    ## Índice de la primera aparición de `sub`, o -1 si no está.
    ## Edge cases: Un `sub` vacío devuelve 0.
    weave index_of with sub as string into int:
        let sv is essence of self
        return calling _index_of_from with sv, sub, 0
    ## Índice de la última aparición de `sub`, o -1 si no está.
    ## Edge cases: Un `sub` vacío devuelve la longitud del string.
    weave last_index_of with sub as string into int:
        let sv is essence of self
        return calling _last_index_of_from with sv, sub, (sv length) - (sub length)
    ## @deprecated Use index_of instead.
    weave find with sub as string into int:
        return calling self.index_of with sub
    ## @deprecated Use last_index_of instead.
    weave rfind with sub as string into int:
        return calling self.last_index_of with sub
    ## Cuenta las apariciones **no solapadas** de `sub`.
    ## Edge cases: Devuelve 0 cuando `sub` está vacío o es más largo.
    weave count with sub as string into int:
        let sv is essence of self
        let sl as int is sub length
        if sl == 0:
            return 0
        var found as int is 0
        var hit as int is calling _index_of_from with sv, sub, 0
        while hit >= 0:
            set found is found + 1
            set hit is calling _index_of_from with sv, sub, hit + sl
        return found
    ## @deprecated Use count instead.
    weave count_matches with sub as string into int:
        return calling self.count with sub

    # --- Corte ----------------------------------------------------------
    ## Substring desde `start_pos` (incluido) hasta `end_pos` (excluido).
    ## Edge cases: `start_pos == end_pos` devuelve ""; los índices van tal cual al runtime.
    weave substring with start_pos as int, end_pos as int into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        return sv at start_pos to end_pos
    ## El byte en `idx` como un string de un carácter.
    weave char_at with idx as int into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        return sv at idx to (idx + 1)
    ## Copia con los bytes en orden inverso.
    weave reverse into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        let ll as int is sv length
        var parts as list of string is list of string with capacity ll
        var i as int is ll - 1
        while i >= 0:
            calling parts.push with (sv at i to (i + 1))
            set i is i - 1
        return calling _concat with parts

    # --- Mayúsculas y minúsculas ---------------------------------------
    ## Copia con las letras ASCII A-Z convertidas a minúsculas.
    weave lower into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        let parts is for ch in sv then calling _lower_char with ch
        return calling _concat with parts
    ## Copia con las letras ASCII a-z convertidas a mayúsculas.
    weave upper into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        let parts is for ch in sv then calling _upper_char with ch
        return calling _concat with parts
    ## @deprecated Use lower instead.
    weave to_lower into string:
        return calling self.lower
    ## @deprecated Use upper instead.
    weave to_upper into string:
        return calling self.upper
    ## Copia con la primera letra en mayúscula y el resto en minúsculas.
    ## Edge cases: Devuelve "" para el string vacío.
    weave capitalize into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        let ll as int is sv length
        if ll == 0:
            return ""
        let head is calling _upper_char with (sv at 0 to 1)
        let lowered is for ch in (sv at 1 to ll) then calling _lower_char with ch
        let tail is calling _concat with lowered
        return "{head}{tail}"
    ## Copia con la inicial de cada palabra en mayúscula y el resto en minúsculas.
    weave title into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        var parts as list of string is list of string with capacity (sv length)
        var at_word_start as bool is true
        for ch in sv:
            if calling _char_is_space with ch:
                calling parts.push with ch
                set at_word_start is true
            else:
                if at_word_start:
                    calling parts.push with (calling _upper_char with ch)
                else:
                    calling parts.push with (calling _lower_char with ch)
                set at_word_start is false
        return calling _concat with parts
    ## @deprecated Use title instead.
    weave title_case into string:
        return calling self.title
    ## Copia con cada letra ASCII cambiada de caja; el resto no cambia.
    weave swap_case into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        let parts is for ch in sv then calling _swap_char with ch
        return calling _concat with parts
    ## Copia en `snake_case`: separa camelCase y normaliza los separadores a `_`.
    ## Edge cases: Colapsa separadores repetidos; "" devuelve "".
    weave to_snake_case into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        var parts as list of string is list of string with capacity (sv length)
        for i, ch in sv:
            if ch == " " or ch == "-" or ch == "_":
                if (parts length) > 0:
                    if (parts at ((parts length) - 1)) != "_":
                        calling parts.push with "_"
            else:
                if calling _char_is_upper with ch:
                    if (parts length) > 0:
                        let prev_is_upper as bool is calling _char_is_upper with (sv at (i - 1))
                        let prev_is_lower as bool is calling _char_is_lower with (sv at (i - 1))
                        let prev_is_digit as bool is calling _char_is_digit with (sv at (i - 1))
                        var next_is_lower as bool is false
                        if (i + 1) < (sv length):
                            set next_is_lower is calling _char_is_lower with (sv at (i + 1))
                        let starts_word as bool is (prev_is_lower or prev_is_digit or (next_is_lower and prev_is_upper))
                        if starts_word and ((parts at ((parts length) - 1)) != "_"):
                            calling parts.push with "_"
                    calling parts.push with (calling _lower_char with ch)
                else:
                    calling parts.push with ch
        return calling _concat with parts
    ## Copia en `kebab-case`: `to_snake_case` con `_` cambiado por `-`.
    weave to_kebab_case into string:
        var snake as string is calling self.to_snake_case
        return calling snake.replace_all with "_", "-"
    ## Forma corta de `to_snake_case`.
    weave snake_case into string:
        return calling self.to_snake_case
    ## Forma corta de `to_kebab_case`.
    weave kebab_case into string:
        return calling self.to_kebab_case
    ## Copia en `PascalCase`: cada palabra de `snake_case` capitalizada.
    ## Edge cases: "" devuelve "".
    weave pascal_case into string:
        var snake as string is calling self.snake_case
        let words_list is calling snake.split with "_"
        var parts as list of string is list of string with capacity (words_list length)
        for word in words_list:
            var piece as string is word
            calling parts.push with (calling piece.capitalize)
        return calling _concat with parts
    ## True cuando todos los bytes son letras ASCII y hay al menos uno.
    weave is_alpha into bool:
        let sv is essence of self
        if (sv length) == 0:
            return false
        for ch in sv:
            if not (calling _char_is_alpha with ch):
                return false
        return true
    ## True cuando todos los bytes son dígitos ASCII y hay al menos uno.
    weave is_digit into bool:
        let sv is essence of self
        if (sv length) == 0:
            return false
        for ch in sv:
            if not (calling _char_is_digit with ch):
                return false
        return true
    ## True cuando todos los bytes son letras o dígitos ASCII y hay al menos uno.
    weave is_alnum into bool:
        let sv is essence of self
        if (sv length) == 0:
            return false
        for ch in sv:
            if not (calling _char_is_alnum with ch):
                return false
        return true
    ## True cuando no hay mayúsculas y hay al menos una minúscula.
    weave is_lower into bool:
        let sv is essence of self
        var has_lower as bool is false
        for ch in sv:
            if calling _char_is_upper with ch:
                return false
            if calling _char_is_lower with ch:
                set has_lower is true
        return has_lower
    ## True cuando no hay minúsculas y hay al menos una mayúscula.
    weave is_upper into bool:
        let sv is essence of self
        var has_upper as bool is false
        for ch in sv:
            if calling _char_is_lower with ch:
                return false
            if calling _char_is_upper with ch:
                set has_upper is true
        return has_upper
    ## True cuando el string se lee igual al derecho y al revés.
    ## Edge cases: Los strings de longitud 0 o 1 son palíndromos.
    weave is_palindrome into bool:
        let sv is essence of self
        let ll as int is sv length
        for i from 0 to (ll / 2):
            if (sv at i to (i + 1)) != (sv at (ll - 1 - i) to (ll - i)):
                return false
        return true

    # --- Espacios -------------------------------------------------------
    ## Copia sin espacios ASCII al principio ni al final.
    weave trim into string:
        var started as string is calling self.trim_start
        return calling started.trim_end
    ## Copia sin espacios ASCII al principio.
    weave trim_start into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        let ll as int is sv length
        var start as int is 0
        while start < ll:
            if calling _char_is_space with (sv at start):
                set start is start + 1
            else:
                break
        return sv at start to ll
    ## Copia sin espacios ASCII al final.
    weave trim_end into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        var end as int is (sv length) - 1
        while end >= 0:
            if calling _char_is_space with (sv at end):
                set end is end - 1
            else:
                break
        return sv at 0 to (end + 1)
    ## @deprecated Use trim_start instead.
    weave lstrip into string:
        return calling self.trim_start
    ## @deprecated Use trim_end instead.
    weave rstrip into string:
        return calling self.trim_end
    ## True cuando el string no está vacío y todos sus bytes son espacios.
    ## Edge cases: Devuelve false para "" (ver `is_blank`).
    weave is_space into bool:
        let sv is essence of self
        if (sv length) == 0:
            return false
        for ch in sv:
            if not (calling _char_is_space with ch):
                return false
        return true
    ## @deprecated Use is_space instead.
    weave is_whitespace into bool:
        return calling self.is_space
    ## True cuando el string está vacío o todos sus bytes son espacios.
    weave is_blank into bool:
        let sv is essence of self
        for ch in sv:
            if not (calling _char_is_space with ch):
                return false
        return true
    ## Lista de palabras separadas por runs de espacios ASCII.
    ## Edge cases: ignora espacios extremos; "" o solo espacios dan lista vacía.
    weave split_whitespace into list of string:
        let sv is essence of self
        var parts as list of string is list of string
        var start as int is -1
        for i, ch in sv:
            if calling _char_is_space with ch:
                if start >= 0:
                    calling parts.push with (sv at start to i)
                    set start is -1
            else:
                if start < 0:
                    set start is i
        if start >= 0:
            calling parts.push with (sv at start to (sv length))
        return parts
    ## Nombre corto de `split_whitespace`.
    weave words into list of string:
        return calling self.split_whitespace
    ## Lista de líneas separadas por `\n`.
    ## Edge cases: "" da lista vacía; un `\n` final añade una línea vacía.
    weave split_lines into list of string:
        var sv as string is essence of self
        if (sv length) == 0:
            return list of string
        let parts is calling sv.split with "\n"
        return parts
    ## Número de líneas separadas por `\n`.
    ## Edge cases: 0 para ""; 1 para un string sin `\n`.
    weave line_count into int:
        let parts is calling self.split_lines
        return parts length
    ## Número de palabras separadas por espacios ASCII.
    weave word_count into int:
        let parts is calling self.words
        return parts length
    ## Lista de líneas con el `\r` final de cada una eliminado (CRLF).
    ## Edge cases: "" da lista vacía; un `\n` final añade una línea vacía.
    weave lines into list of string:
        let raw is calling self.split_lines
        var parts as list of string is list of string with capacity (raw length)
        for line in raw:
            var clean_line as string is line
            calling parts.push with (calling clean_line.removesuffix with "\r")
        return parts

    # --- Reemplazo y división ------------------------------------------
    ## Copia con la primera aparición de `from_str` sustituida por `to_str`.
    ## Edge cases: un `from_str` vacío inserta `to_str` al principio (legado).
    weave replace with from_str as string, to_str as string into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        let hit as int is calling _index_of_from with sv, from_str, 0
        if hit < 0:
            return sv
        let fl as int is from_str length
        let head is sv at 0 to hit
        let tail is sv at (hit + fl) to (sv length)
        return "{head}{to_str}{tail}"
    ## Copia con **todas** las apariciones no solapadas de `from_str`
    ## Edge cases: Un `from_str` vacío devuelve el string sin cambios.
    weave replace_all with from_str as string, to_str as string into string:
        let parts is calling self.split with from_str
        return calling _join_parts with parts, to_str
    ## Divide por cada aparición de `delim`.
    ## Edge cases: Un `delim` vacío devuelve una lista con el string entero.
    weave split with delim as string into list of string:
        let sv is essence of self
        let dl as int is delim length
        var parts as list of string is list of string
        if dl == 0:
            calling parts.push with sv
            return parts
        var start as int is 0
        var hit as int is calling _index_of_from with sv, delim, start
        while hit >= 0:
            calling parts.push with (sv at start to hit)
            set start is hit + dl
            set hit is calling _index_of_from with sv, delim, start
        calling parts.push with (sv at start to (sv length))
        return parts
    ## Divide en la **primera** aparición de `sep`: `[antes, sep, después]`.
    ## Edge cases: si `sep` falta o está vacío devuelve `[self, "", ""]`.
    weave partition with sep as string into list of string:
        let sv is essence of self
        var parts as list of string is list of string with capacity 3
        let hit as int is calling _index_of_from with sv, sep, 0
        if hit < 0 or (sep length) == 0:
            calling parts.push with sv
            calling parts.push with ""
            calling parts.push with ""
            return parts
        let sl as int is sep length
        calling parts.push with (sv at 0 to hit)
        calling parts.push with sep
        calling parts.push with (sv at (hit + sl) to (sv length))
        return parts
    ## Copia repetida `count` veces.
    ## Edge cases: `count <= 0` o string vacío devuelven "".
    weave repeat with count as int into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        if count <= 0 or (sv length) == 0:
            return ""
        var parts as list of string is list of string with capacity count
        for i from 0 to count:
            calling parts.push with sv
        return calling _concat with parts
    ## Copia repetida `count` veces y unida con `sep`.
    ## Edge cases: `count <= 0` o string vacío devuelven "".
    weave repeat_join with count as int, sep as string into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        if count <= 0 or (sv length) == 0:
            return ""
        var parts as list of string is list of string with capacity count
        for i from 0 to count:
            calling parts.push with sv
        return calling _join_parts with parts, sep

    # --- Alineación -----------------------------------------------------
    ## Alinea a la izquierda en `width`, rellenando por la derecha con `pad_char`.
    ## Edge cases: si ya cabe o `pad_char` está vacío no cambia; se recorta a `width`.
    weave ljust with width as int, pad_char as string is " " into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        let ll as int is sv length
        let pl as int is pad_char length
        if ll >= width or pl == 0:
            return sv
        let pad_count as int is ((width - ll) + pl - 1) / pl
        let padded is calling _pad_right with sv, pad_count, pad_char
        if (padded length) > width:
            return padded at 0 to width
        return padded
    ## Alinea a la derecha en `width`, rellenando por la izquierda con `pad_char`.
    weave rjust with width as int, pad_char as string is " " into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        let ll as int is sv length
        let pl as int is pad_char length
        if ll >= width or pl == 0:
            return sv
        let pad_count as int is ((width - ll) + pl - 1) / pl
        let padded is calling _pad_left with sv, pad_count, pad_char
        if (padded length) > width:
            return padded at ((padded length) - width) to (padded length)
        return padded
    ## @deprecated Use rjust instead.
    weave pad_left with width as int, pad_char as string is " " into string:
        return calling self.rjust with width, pad_char
    ## @deprecated Use ljust instead.
    weave pad_right with width as int, pad_char as string is " " into string:
        return calling self.ljust with width, pad_char
    ## Rellena con ceros por la izquierda hasta `width`, conservando el signo.
    weave zfill with width as int into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        if (sv length) >= width:
            return sv
        var sign as string is ""
        var rest as string is sv
        if (sv length) > 0:
            let first is sv at 0 to 1
            if first == "-" or first == "+":
                set sign is first
                set rest is sv at 1 to (sv length)
        let zeros as int is width - (rest length) - (sign length)
        let padded is calling _pad_left with rest, zeros, "0"
        return "{sign}{padded}"
    ## Centra en un campo de `width` rellenando con `pad_char`.
    ## Edge cases: con relleno impar la izquierda recibe la mitad menor (Python).
    weave center with width as int, pad_char as string is " " into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        let ll as int is sv length
        if ll >= width or (pad_char length) == 0:
            return sv
        let total as int is width - ll
        let left_count as int is total / 2
        let right_count as int is total - left_count
        let left_pad is calling _pad_left with "", left_count, pad_char
        let right_pad is calling _pad_right with "", right_count, pad_char
        return "{left_pad}{sv}{right_pad}"

    # --- Prefijos y sufijos --------------------------------------------
    ## Copia con `prefix` eliminado del principio si está presente.
    weave removeprefix with prefix as string into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        if calling _has_prefix_at with sv, prefix, 0:
            return sv at (prefix length) to (sv length)
        return sv
    ## Copia con `suffix` eliminado del final si está presente.
    weave removesuffix with suffix as string into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        let ll as int is sv length
        let sl as int is suffix length
        if sl <= ll:
            if calling _has_prefix_at with sv, suffix, ll - sl:
                return sv at 0 to (ll - sl)
        return sv

    # --- Comparación ----------------------------------------------------
    ## Compara byte a byte con `other` y devuelve -1, 0 o 1.
    weave compare with other as string into int:
        let sv is essence of self
        let l1 as int is sv length
        let l2 as int is other length
        let min_l is if l1 < l2 then l1 else l2
        for i from 0 to min_l:
            let c1 as int is ord (sv at i)
            let c2 as int is ord (other at i)
            if c1 != c2:
                return if c1 < c2 then -1 else 1
        return if l1 < l2 then -1 else (if l1 > l2 then 1 else 0)
    # --- Truncado -------------------------------------------------------
    ## Recorta a `max_len` bytes añadiendo `suffix` si hubo recorte.
    ## Edge cases: `max_len <= len(suffix)` recorta sin sufijo; `max_len <= 0` da "".
    weave truncate with max_len as int, suffix as string into string:
        let sv is essence of self
        let ll as int is sv length
        if ll <= max_len:
            return sv
        let sl as int is suffix length
        if max_len <= sl:
            if max_len <= 0:
                return ""
            return sv at 0 to max_len
        let head is sv at 0 to (max_len - sl)
        return "{head}{suffix}"
    ## Recorta a `max_len` bytes añadiendo "..." si hubo recorte.
    weave ellipsis with max_len as int into string:
        return calling self.truncate with max_len, "..."

    # --- Parseo ---------------------------------------------------------
    ## Interpreta el string como entero (con espacios y signo opcionales).
    weave parse_int into maybe int:
        let sv is essence of self
        return calling spark.parse_int with sv
    ## True cuando el string es un literal numérico exacto: signo y `.` opcionales.
    weave is_numeric into bool:
        let sv is essence of self
        var has_digit as bool is false
        var has_dot as bool is false
        for i, ch in sv:
            if ch == "+" or ch == "-":
                if i != 0:
                    return false
            else:
                if ch == ".":
                    if has_dot:
                        return false
                    set has_dot is true
                else:
                    if calling _char_is_digit with ch:
                        set has_digit is true
                    else:
                        return false
        return has_digit
    ## Interpreta el string como decimal (con espacios; sin exponentes).
    weave parse_float into maybe float:
        var sv as string is essence of self
        var trimmed as string is calling sv.trim
        if not (calling trimmed.is_numeric):
            return maybe none
        return some (calling _float_from_literal with trimmed)
# --- Funciones de módulo ------------------------------------------------
# Forma funcional de cada método: el receptor pasa a ser el primer
# parámetro `s` y el `weave` delega en el método homónimo, que está
# documentado arriba. El contrato y los bordes son idénticos.
weave len with s as string into int:
    return calling s.len
weave is_empty with s as string into bool:
    return calling s.is_empty
weave contains with s as string, sub as string into bool:
    return calling s.contains with sub
weave starts_with with s as string, prefix as string into bool:
    return calling s.starts_with with prefix
weave ends_with with s as string, suffix as string into bool:
    return calling s.ends_with with suffix
weave index_of with s as string, sub as string into int:
    return calling s.index_of with sub
weave last_index_of with s as string, sub as string into int:
    return calling s.last_index_of with sub
weave substring with s as string, start_pos as int, end_pos as int into string:
    return calling s.substring with start_pos, end_pos
weave char_at with s as string, idx as int into string:
    return calling s.char_at with idx
weave lower with s as string into string:
    return calling s.lower
weave upper with s as string into string:
    return calling s.upper
weave to_lower with s as string into string:
    return calling s.to_lower
weave to_upper with s as string into string:
    return calling s.to_upper
weave trim with s as string into string:
    return calling s.trim
weave trim_start with s as string into string:
    return calling s.trim_start
weave trim_end with s as string into string:
    return calling s.trim_end
weave replace with s as string, from_str as string, to_str as string into string:
    return calling s.replace with from_str, to_str
weave replace_all with s as string, from_str as string, to_str as string into string:
    return calling s.replace_all with from_str, to_str
weave split with s as string, delim as string into list of string:
    return calling s.split with delim
weave repeat with s as string, count as int into string:
    return calling s.repeat with count
weave repeat_join with s as string, count as int, sep as string into string:
    return calling s.repeat_join with count, sep
weave reverse with s as string into string:
    return calling s.reverse
weave is_alpha with s as string into bool:
    return calling s.is_alpha
weave is_digit with s as string into bool:
    return calling s.is_digit
weave is_alnum with s as string into bool:
    return calling s.is_alnum
weave capitalize with s as string into string:
    return calling s.capitalize
weave title with s as string into string:
    return calling s.title
weave title_case with s as string into string:
    return calling s.title_case
weave swap_case with s as string into string:
    return calling s.swap_case
weave to_snake_case with s as string into string:
    return calling s.to_snake_case
weave to_kebab_case with s as string into string:
    return calling s.to_kebab_case
weave snake_case with s as string into string:
    return calling s.snake_case
weave kebab_case with s as string into string:
    return calling s.kebab_case
weave pascal_case with s as string into string:
    return calling s.pascal_case
weave find with s as string, sub as string into int:
    return calling s.find with sub
weave rfind with s as string, sub as string into int:
    return calling s.rfind with sub
weave count with s as string, sub as string into int:
    return calling s.count with sub
weave count_matches with s as string, sub as string into int:
    return calling s.count_matches with sub
weave lstrip with s as string into string:
    return calling s.lstrip
weave rstrip with s as string into string:
    return calling s.rstrip
weave is_space with s as string into bool:
    return calling s.is_space
weave is_whitespace with s as string into bool:
    return calling s.is_whitespace
weave is_blank with s as string into bool:
    return calling s.is_blank
weave split_whitespace with s as string into list of string:
    return calling s.split_whitespace
weave words with s as string into list of string:
    return calling s.words
weave split_lines with s as string into list of string:
    return calling s.split_lines
weave lines with s as string into list of string:
    return calling s.lines
weave line_count with s as string into int:
    return calling s.line_count
weave word_count with s as string into int:
    return calling s.word_count
weave ljust with s as string, width as int, pad_char as string is " " into string:
    return calling s.ljust with width, pad_char
weave rjust with s as string, width as int, pad_char as string is " " into string:
    return calling s.rjust with width, pad_char
weave pad_left with s as string, width as int, pad_char as string is " " into string:
    return calling s.pad_left with width, pad_char
weave pad_right with s as string, width as int, pad_char as string is " " into string:
    return calling s.pad_right with width, pad_char
weave zfill with s as string, width as int into string:
    return calling s.zfill with width
weave center with s as string, width as int, pad_char as string is " " into string:
    return calling s.center with width, pad_char
weave removeprefix with s as string, prefix as string into string:
    return calling s.removeprefix with prefix
weave removesuffix with s as string, suffix as string into string:
    return calling s.removesuffix with suffix
weave partition with s as string, sep as string into list of string:
    return calling s.partition with sep
weave is_lower with s as string into bool:
    return calling s.is_lower
weave is_upper with s as string into bool:
    return calling s.is_upper
weave is_palindrome with s as string into bool:
    return calling s.is_palindrome
weave compare with a as string, b as string into int:
    return calling a.compare with b
weave chars with s as string into list of string:
    return calling s.chars
weave bytes with s as string into list of int:
    return calling s.bytes
weave truncate with s as string, max_len as int, suffix as string into string:
    return calling s.truncate with max_len, suffix
weave ellipsis with s as string, max_len as int into string:
    return calling s.ellipsis with max_len
weave is_numeric with s as string into bool:
    return calling s.is_numeric

## Une los elementos de `parts` con `sep` entre ellos.
##
## ## Ownership
## Devuelve un `string` nuevo y auto-banishable.
##
## Edge cases: Una lista vacía devuelve "".
weave join with parts as list of string, sep as string into string:
    return calling _join_parts with parts, sep

# --- Helpers privados ----------------------------------------------------
## Une `parts` con `sep` entre elementos (cuerpo real de `join`).
weave _join_parts with parts as list of string, sep as string into string:
    let ll as int is parts length
    if ll == 0:
        return ""
    var pieces as list of string is list of string with capacity ll
    calling pieces.push with (parts at 0)
    var i as int is 1
    while i < ll:
        calling pieces.push with "{sep}{parts at i}"
        set i is i + 1
    return calling _concat with pieces
## Único punto de acumulación de strings del módulo: une `parts` tal cual.
weave _concat with parts as list of string into string:
    var out as string is ""
    for part in parts:
        set out is "{out}{part}"
    return out
## True cuando `ch` es un espacio ASCII: espacio, tab, LF, CR, VT o FF.
weave _char_is_space with ch as string into bool:
    return ch == " " or ch == "\t" or ch == "\n" or ch == "\r" or ch == "\v" or ch == "\f"
## True cuando `ch` es un dígito ASCII (0-9).
weave _char_is_digit with ch as string into bool:
    let code as int is ord ch
    return code >= 48 and code <= 57
## True cuando `ch` es una letra ASCII mayúscula (A-Z).
weave _char_is_upper with ch as string into bool:
    let code as int is ord ch
    return code >= 65 and code <= 90
## True cuando `ch` es una letra ASCII minúscula (a-z).
weave _char_is_lower with ch as string into bool:
    let code as int is ord ch
    return code >= 97 and code <= 122
## True cuando `ch` es una letra ASCII (A-Z o a-z).
weave _char_is_alpha with ch as string into bool:
    if calling _char_is_upper with ch:
        return true
    return calling _char_is_lower with ch
## True cuando `ch` es una letra o un dígito ASCII.
weave _char_is_alnum with ch as string into bool:
    if calling _char_is_alpha with ch:
        return true
    return calling _char_is_digit with ch
## Copia de `ch` en minúscula si es una letra ASCII mayúscula.
weave _lower_char with ch as string into string:
    if calling _char_is_upper with ch:
        return chr ((ord ch) + 32)
    return ch
## Copia de `ch` en mayúscula si es una letra ASCII minúscula.
weave _upper_char with ch as string into string:
    if calling _char_is_lower with ch:
        return chr ((ord ch) - 32)
    return ch
## Copia de `ch` con la caja ASCII cambiada.
weave _swap_char with ch as string into string:
    if calling _char_is_upper with ch:
        return chr ((ord ch) + 32)
    if calling _char_is_lower with ch:
        return chr ((ord ch) - 32)
    return ch
## True cuando `s` contiene `prefix` a partir de la posición `pos`.
weave _has_prefix_at with s as string, prefix as string, pos as int into bool:
    let pl as int is prefix length
    if pos < 0:
        return false
    if (pos + pl) > (s length):
        return false
    return (s at pos to (pos + pl)) == prefix
## Primera posición de `sub` en `s` a partir de `from_pos` (incluido), o -1.
weave _index_of_from with s as string, sub as string, from_pos as int into int:
    let ll as int is s length
    let sl as int is sub length
    if sl == 0:
        return 0
    if sl > ll:
        return -1
    var i as int is from_pos
    if i < 0:
        set i is 0
    while i <= ll - sl:
        if calling _has_prefix_at with s, sub, i:
            return i
        set i is i + 1
    return -1
## Última posición de `sub` en `s` en o antes de `from_pos`, o -1.
weave _last_index_of_from with s as string, sub as string, from_pos as int into int:
    if (sub length) == 0:
        return s length
    var i as int is from_pos
    while i >= 0:
        if calling _has_prefix_at with s, sub, i:
            return i
        set i is i - 1
    return -1
## Copia de `s` con `count` copias de `pad_char` delante.
weave _pad_left with s as string, count as int, pad_char as string into string:
    if count <= 0:
        return s
    var parts as list of string is list of string with capacity (count + 1)
    for i from 0 to count:
        calling parts.push with pad_char
    calling parts.push with s
    return calling _concat with parts
## Copia de `s` con `count` copias de `pad_char` detrás.
weave _pad_right with s as string, count as int, pad_char as string into string:
    if count <= 0:
        return s
    var parts as list of string is list of string with capacity (count + 1)
    calling parts.push with s
    for i from 0 to count:
        calling parts.push with pad_char
    return calling _concat with parts
## Valor decimal de un literal numérico válido (precondición: `is_numeric`).
weave _float_from_literal with s as string into float:
    var int_val as float is 0.0
    var frac_val as float is 0.0
    var scale as float is 1.0
    var seen_dot as bool is false
    for ch in s:
        if ch == ".":
            set seen_dot is true
        else:
            if calling _char_is_digit with ch:
                let digit as float is ((ord ch) - 48) to float
                if seen_dot:
                    set scale is scale * 10.0
                    set frac_val is (frac_val * 10.0) + digit
                else:
                    set int_val is (int_val * 10.0) + digit
    var sign as float is 1.0
    if (s at 0 to 1) == "-":
        set sign is -1.0
    return sign * (int_val + (frac_val / scale))
## Harness privado de tests: panickea con `label` cuando `cond` es falso.
weave _expect with cond as bool, label as string into void:
    if not cond:
        calling spark.panic with "scrolls test failed: {label}"
## Harness privado de tests: igualdad de enteros.
weave _expect_eq_int with actual as int, expected as int, label as string into void:
    if actual != expected:
        calling spark.panic with "scrolls test failed: {label}: {(actual to string)} != {(expected to string)}"
## Harness privado de tests: igualdad de strings.
weave _expect_eq_string with actual as string, expected as string, label as string into void:
    if actual != expected:
        calling spark.panic with "scrolls test failed: {label}: {actual} != {expected}"
## Harness privado de tests: igualdad de booleanos.
weave _expect_eq_bool with actual as bool, expected as bool, label as string into void:
    if actual != expected:
        calling spark.panic with "scrolls test failed: {label}"
# --- Tests ---
# Harness privado en `_expect*` (ver `## Notas de diseño`).

# Longitud e iteración
test "len cuenta bytes, también en UTF-8":
    var s as string is "café"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling s.len), 5, "len"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling len with "abc"), 3, "len func"
test "is_empty distingue el string vacío":
    var vacio as string is ""
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling vacio.is_empty), true, "is_empty"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_empty with "x"), false, "is_empty func"
test "chars devuelve un string de un byte por elemento":
    var s as string is "abc"
    var partes as list of string is calling s.chars
    calling _expect_eq_int with (partes length), 3, "chars"
    var letras as list of string is calling chars with s
    calling _expect_eq_string with (letras at 1), "b", "chars func"
test "bytes devuelve los códigos ASCII":
    var s as string is "AB"
    var codigos as list of int is calling s.bytes
    calling _expect_eq_int with (codigos at 0), 65, "bytes"
    var codigos_func as list of int is calling bytes with s
    calling _expect_eq_int with (codigos_func at 1), 66, "bytes func"

# Búsqueda
test "contains encuentra y descarta substrings":
    var s as string is "abc"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling s.contains with "bc"), true, "contains"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling contains with s, "z"), false, "contains func"
test "starts_with acepta el prefijo vacío":
    var s as string is "abc"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling s.starts_with with ""), true, "prefijo vacío"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling starts_with with s, "bc"), false, "prefijo erróneo"
test "ends_with reconoce sufijos":
    var s as string is "abc"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling s.ends_with with "bc"), true, "ends_with"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling ends_with with s, "abcd"), false, "sufijo largo"
test "index_of devuelve la primera posición":
    var s as string is "abracadabra"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling s.index_of with "cad"), 4, "index_of"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling index_of with s, ""), 0, "sub vacío"
test "index_of devuelve -1 cuando no encuentra":
    var s as string is "abc"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling s.index_of with "z"), -1, "ausente"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling s.index_of with "abcd"), -1, "más largo"
test "last_index_of devuelve la última posición":
    var s as string is "abracadabra"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling s.last_index_of with "abra"), 7, "last_index_of"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling last_index_of with s, "z"), -1, "ausente"
test "last_index_of con sub vacío devuelve la longitud":
    var s as string is "abc"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling s.last_index_of with ""), 3, "sub vacío"
test "count cuenta apariciones no solapadas":
    var s as string is "abracadabra"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling s.count with "a"), 5, "count"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling count with s, "abra"), 2, "count func"
test "count ignora el sub vacío y el sub más largo":
    var s as string is "abc"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling s.count with ""), 0, "vacío"
    var repetido as string is "aaaa"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling repetido.count with "aa"), 2, "no solapado"
test "find, rfind y count_matches siguen funcionando":
    var s as string is "abracadabra"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling s.find with "cad"), 4, "find"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling s.rfind with "abra"), 7, "rfind"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling s.count_matches with "a"), 5, "count_matches"
test "formas funcionales de consulta":
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling contains with "abc", "b"), true, "contains"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling starts_with with "abc", "ab"), true, "starts_with"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling ends_with with "abc", "bc"), true, "ends_with"
test "formas funcionales de posición y recuento":
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling index_of with "abc", "c"), 2, "index_of"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling last_index_of with "abca", "a"), 3, "last_index_of"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling count_matches with "aaaa", "aa"), 2, "count_matches"

# Corte
test "substring corta el rango pedido":
    var s as string is "abcdef"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.substring with 1, 4), "bcd", "substring"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling substring with s, 0, 0), "", "rango vacío"
test "char_at devuelve un byte como string":
    var s as string is "abc"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.char_at with 1), "b", "char_at"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling char_at with s, 2), "c", "char_at func"
test "reverse invierte el orden de los bytes":
    var s as string is "pengu"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.reverse), "ugnep", "reverse"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling reverse with s), "ugnep", "reverse func"
test "reverse del string vacío devuelve vacío":
    var vacio as string is ""
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling vacio.reverse), "", "reverse vacío"

# Caja
test "lower convierte A-Z y no toca el resto":
    var s as string is "Hello, World!"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.lower), "hello, world!", "lower"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling lower with s), "hello, world!", "lower func"
test "upper convierte a-z a mayúsculas":
    var s as string is "abc"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.upper), "ABC", "upper"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling upper with s), "ABC", "upper func"
test "to_lower y to_upper siguen funcionando":
    var s as string is "AbC"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.to_lower), "abc", "to_lower"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling to_upper with s), "ABC", "to_upper func"
test "lower deja intactos los bytes UTF-8":
    var s as string is "CAFé"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.lower), "café", "UTF-8"
test "capitalize deja solo la primera letra en mayúscula":
    var s as string is "hELLO world"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.capitalize), "Hello world", "capitalize"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling capitalize with "1abc"), "1abc", "dígito inicial"
test "capitalize del string vacío devuelve vacío":
    var vacio as string is ""
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling vacio.capitalize), "", "capitalize vacío"
test "title capitaliza la inicial de cada palabra":
    var s as string is "hello world"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.title), "Hello World", "title"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling title with s), "Hello World", "title func"
test "title conserva el espaciado original":
    var s as string is "  a  b "
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.title), "  A  B ", "espacios"
test "title_case sigue funcionando":
    var s as string is "hello world"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.title_case), "Hello World", "title_case"
test "swap_case cambia la caja de cada letra":
    var s as string is "Hello, World!"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.swap_case), "hELLO, wORLD!", "swap_case"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling swap_case with "a1B"), "A1b", "no letras"
test "to_snake_case separa camelCase y PascalCase":
    var s as string is "helloWorld"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.to_snake_case), "hello_world", "camel"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling to_snake_case with "HTTPServer"), "http_server", "siglas"
test "to_snake_case normaliza separadores":
    var s as string is "hello--world"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.to_snake_case), "hello_world", "guiones"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling to_snake_case with ""), "", "vacío"
test "to_kebab_case usa guiones":
    var s as string is "HelloWorld"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.to_kebab_case), "hello-world", "kebab"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling to_kebab_case with s), "hello-world", "kebab func"
test "snake_case y kebab_case son formas cortas":
    var s as string is "helloWorld"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.snake_case), "hello_world", "snake_case"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling kebab_case with s), "hello-world", "kebab_case func"
test "pascal_case capitaliza cada palabra":
    var s as string is "hello_world"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.pascal_case), "HelloWorld", "snake a pascal"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling pascal_case with "helloWorld"), "HelloWorld", "func"
test "is_alpha exige solo letras ASCII":
    var s as string is "aB"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling s.is_alpha), true, "is_alpha"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_alpha with "a1"), false, "con dígito"
test "is_digit exige solo dígitos ASCII":
    var s as string is "123"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling s.is_digit), true, "is_digit"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_digit with "12a"), false, "con letra"
test "is_alnum acepta letras y dígitos":
    var s as string is "a1"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling s.is_alnum), true, "is_alnum"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_alnum with "a 1"), false, "con espacio"
test "is_lower e is_upper ignoran lo no alfabético":
    var s as string is "a1"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling s.is_lower), true, "is_lower"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_upper with "A1"), true, "is_upper"
test "is_palindrome detecta palíndromos":
    var s as string is "racecar"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling s.is_palindrome), true, "palíndromo"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_palindrome with "ab"), false, "no palíndromo"
test "formas funcionales de caja":
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling capitalize with "hOLA"), "Hola", "capitalize"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling title with "a b"), "A B", "title"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling swap_case with "aB"), "Ab", "swap_case"
test "formas funcionales de conversión de estilo":
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling to_snake_case with "aB"), "a_b", "to_snake_case"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling to_kebab_case with "aB"), "a-b", "to_kebab_case"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling snake_case with "aB"), "a_b", "snake_case"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling pascal_case with "a_b"), "AB", "pascal_case"
test "formas funcionales de caja antigua":
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling to_lower with "AbC"), "abc", "to_lower"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling to_upper with "AbC"), "ABC", "to_upper"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling title_case with "a b"), "A B", "title_case"

# Espacios
test "trim quita espacios ASCII de los extremos":
    var s as string is "\t\n x \r\v\f "
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.trim), "x", "trim"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling trim with "  a  "), "a", "trim func"
test "trim_start quita solo el principio":
    var s as string is "  a  "
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.trim_start), "a  ", "trim_start"
test "trim_end quita solo el final":
    var s as string is "  a  "
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.trim_end), "  a", "trim_end"
test "lstrip y rstrip siguen funcionando":
    var s as string is "  a  "
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.lstrip), "a  ", "lstrip"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling rstrip with s), "  a", "rstrip func"
test "is_space es false para el string vacío":
    var vacio as string is ""
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling vacio.is_space), false, "vacío"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_space with "   "), true, "solo espacios"
test "is_whitespace sigue funcionando":
    var s as string is "\t\n"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling s.is_whitespace), true, "is_whitespace"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_whitespace with " x"), false, "con texto"
test "is_blank es true para vacío o solo espacios":
    var vacio as string is ""
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling vacio.is_blank), true, "vacío"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_blank with "a"), false, "con texto"
test "split_whitespace ignora espacios repetidos":
    var s as string is "  a  b "
    var partes as list of string is calling s.split_whitespace
    calling _expect_eq_int with (partes length), 2, "split_whitespace"
    var palabras_func as list of string is calling split_whitespace with s
    calling _expect_eq_string with (palabras_func at 0), "a", "func"
test "words es la forma corta de split_whitespace":
    var s as string is "a\tb\nc"
    calling _expect_eq_int with ((calling s.words) length), 3, "words"
    calling _expect_eq_int with ((calling words with "   ") length), 0, "solo espacios"
test "split_lines divide por salto de línea y conserva el CR":
    var s as string is "a\r\nb"
    var partes as list of string is calling s.split_lines
    calling _expect_eq_int with (partes length), 2, "split_lines"
    var lineas_func as list of string is calling split_lines with s
    calling _expect_eq_string with (lineas_func at 0), "a\r", "func"
test "lines elimina el CR final de cada línea":
    var s as string is "a\r\nb\nc"
    var partes as list of string is calling s.lines
    calling _expect_eq_int with (partes length), 3, "lines"
    var limpias_func as list of string is calling lines with s
    calling _expect_eq_string with (limpias_func at 0), "a", "func"
test "line_count cuenta líneas separadas por LF":
    var s as string is "a\nb\nc"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling s.line_count), 3, "line_count"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling line_count with ""), 0, "vacío"
test "word_count cuenta palabras separadas por espacios":
    var s as string is "  a  b "
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling s.word_count), 2, "word_count"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling word_count with "abc"), 1, "una palabra"
test "formas funcionales de espacios":
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling trim_start with " a"), "a", "trim_start"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling trim_end with "a "), "a", "trim_end"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling lstrip with " a"), "a", "lstrip"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling rstrip with "a "), "a", "rstrip"
test "formas funcionales de división por espacios":
    calling _expect_eq_int with ((calling split_whitespace with "a b") length), 2, "split_whitespace"
    calling _expect_eq_int with ((calling words with "a b") length), 2, "words"
    calling _expect_eq_int with ((calling lines with "a\nb") length), 2, "lines"
    calling _expect_eq_int with ((calling split_lines with "a\nb") length), 2, "split_lines"
test "formas funcionales de recuento de líneas y palabras":
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling line_count with "a\nb"), 2, "line_count"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling word_count with "a b"), 2, "word_count"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_whitespace with " "), true, "is_whitespace"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_blank with ""), true, "is_blank"

# Reemplazo y división
test "replace sustituye solo la primera aparición":
    var s as string is "cat, dog, cat"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.replace with "cat", "bird"), "bird, dog, cat", "replace"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling replace with s, "cat", "bird"), "bird, dog, cat", "func"
test "replace sin coincidencia no cambia el string":
    var s as string is "abc"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.replace with "z", "x"), "abc", "sin coincidencia"
test "replace con from_str vacío inserta al principio":
    var s as string is "abc"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.replace with "", "X"), "Xabc", "legado"
test "replace_all sustituye todas las apariciones":
    var s as string is "cat, dog, cat"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.replace_all with "cat", "bird"), "bird, dog, bird", "replace_all"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling replace_all with s, "cat", "bird"), "bird, dog, bird", "func"
test "replace_all con from_str vacío no cambia":
    var s as string is "abc"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.replace_all with "", "X"), "abc", "vacío"
test "split divide por cada delimitador":
    var s as string is "a,,b"
    var partes as list of string is calling s.split with ","
    calling _expect_eq_int with (partes length), 3, "split"
    var trozos_func as list of string is calling split with s, ","
    calling _expect_eq_string with (trozos_func at 1), "", "func"
test "split con delimitador vacío devuelve el string entero":
    var s as string is "abc"
    var partes as list of string is calling s.split with ""
    calling _expect_eq_int with (partes length), 1, "split vacío"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (partes at 0), "abc", "contenido"
test "split con delimitador ausente devuelve un elemento":
    var s as string is "abc"
    var partes as list of string is calling s.split with "::"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (partes length), 1, "ausente"
test "split acepta delimitadores multi-byte":
    var s as string is "a::b::c"
    var partes as list of string is calling s.split with "::"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (partes length), 3, "multi-char"
test "partition devuelve antes, separador y después":
    var s as string is "a=b=c"
    var partes as list of string is calling s.partition with "="
    calling _expect_eq_int with (partes length), 3, "partition"
    var partes_func as list of string is calling partition with s, "="
    calling _expect_eq_string with (partes_func at 2), "b=c", "func"
test "partition sin separador devuelve el string y dos vacíos":
    var s as string is "abc"
    var partes as list of string is calling s.partition with "="
    calling _expect_eq_string with (partes at 0), "abc", "sin sep"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (partes at 1), "", "vacío"
test "repeat repite el string count veces":
    var s as string is "ha"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.repeat with 3), "hahaha", "repeat"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling repeat with s, 1), "ha", "repeat func"
test "repeat con count no positivo devuelve vacío":
    var s as string is "ha"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.repeat with 0), "", "cero"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.repeat with -1), "", "negativo"
test "repeat_join une las repeticiones con el separador":
    var s as string is "ab"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.repeat_join with 3, ", "), "ab, ab, ab", "repeat_join"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling repeat_join with s, 1, ","), "ab", "una copia"
test "formas funcionales de reemplazo y división":
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling replace with "abc", "b", "X"), "aXc", "replace"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling replace_all with "abc", "", "X"), "abc", "replace_all"
    calling _expect_eq_int with ((calling split with "a,b", ",") length), 2, "split"
    calling _expect_eq_int with ((calling partition with "a=b", "=") length), 3, "partition"

# Alineación
test "ljust rellena por la derecha":
    var s as string is "ab"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.ljust with 4, "."), "ab..", "ljust"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling ljust with s, 4, "."), "ab..", "ljust func"
test "ljust no cambia lo que ya cabe y respeta pad_char vacío":
    var s as string is "abc"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.ljust with 2, "."), "abc", "ya cabe"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.ljust with 5, ""), "abc", "pad vacío"
test "ljust recorta cuando el relleno multi-carácter se pasa":
    var s as string is "ab"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.ljust with 5, "xy"), "abxyx", "recorte"
test "rjust rellena por la izquierda":
    var s as string is "42"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.rjust with 5, "0"), "00042", "rjust"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling rjust with s, 5, "0"), "00042", "rjust func"
test "rjust recorta cuando el relleno multi-carácter se pasa":
    var s as string is "ab"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.rjust with 5, "xy"), "yxyab", "recorte"
test "pad_left y pad_right siguen funcionando":
    var s as string is "42"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.pad_left with 5, "0"), "00042", "pad_left"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling pad_right with "ab", 4, "."), "ab..", "pad_right"
test "zfill rellena con ceros por la izquierda":
    var s as string is "42"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.zfill with 5), "00042", "zfill"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling zfill with s, 5), "00042", "zfill func"
test "zfill conserva el signo y no toca lo que ya cabe":
    var a as string is "-42"
    var b as string is "+42"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling a.zfill with 6), "-00042", "negativo"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling b.zfill with 5), "+0042", "positivo"
test "center reparte el relleno a ambos lados":
    var s as string is "42"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.center with 6, "-"), "--42--", "center"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling center with s, 6, "-"), "--42--", "center func"
test "center deja la mitad menor a la izquierda":
    var s as string is "ab"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.center with 5, "-"), "-ab--", "impar"
test "center con pad multi-carácter no recorta":
    var s as string is "ab"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.center with 6, "xy"), "xyxyabxyxy", "multi-char"
test "formas funcionales de alineación":
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling ljust with "ab", 4), "ab  ", "ljust"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling rjust with "ab", 4), "  ab", "rjust"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling zfill with "7", 3), "007", "zfill"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling center with "a", 3, "."), ".a.", "center"

# Prefijos y sufijos
test "removeprefix quita el prefijo si está":
    var s as string is "Hello"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.removeprefix with "He"), "llo", "removeprefix"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling removeprefix with s, ""), "Hello", "prefijo vacío"
test "removeprefix no cambia si no coincide":
    var s as string is "Hello"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.removeprefix with "x"), "Hello", "sin coincidencia"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.removeprefix with "Hello!"), "Hello", "más largo"
test "removesuffix quita el sufijo si está":
    var s as string is "Hello"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.removesuffix with "lo"), "Hel", "removesuffix"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling removesuffix with s, ""), "Hello", "sufijo vacío"
test "removesuffix no cambia si no coincide":
    var s as string is "Hello"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.removesuffix with "x"), "Hello", "sin coincidencia"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.removesuffix with "Hello!"), "Hello", "más largo"

# Comparación
test "compare ordena lexicográficamente por byte":
    var a as string is "apple"
    var b as string is "banana"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling a.compare with b), -1, "menor"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling compare with b, a), 1, "func mayor"
test "compare usa la longitud como desempate":
    var a as string is "ab"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling a.compare with "abc"), -1, "prefijo menor"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling a.compare with ""), 1, "contra vacío"
test "compare devuelve 0 para strings iguales":
    var a as string is "abc"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling a.compare with "abc"), 0, "iguales"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling compare with "", ""), 0, "vacíos"
test "compare distingue mayúsculas de minúsculas":
    var a as string is "a"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling a.compare with "A"), 1, "byte mayor"

# Truncado
test "truncate añade el sufijo al recortar":
    var s as string is "Hello, PenguScript!"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.truncate with 10, "..."), "Hello, ...", "truncate"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling truncate with s, 10, "..."), "Hello, ...", "func"
test "truncate no cambia lo que ya cabe":
    var s as string is "abc"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.truncate with 10, "..."), "abc", "sin recorte"
test "truncate con max_len pequeño corta sin sufijo":
    var s as string is "abcdef"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.truncate with 3, "..."), "abc", "sin sufijo"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.truncate with 0, "..."), "", "cero"
test "ellipsis recorta añadiendo puntos suspensivos":
    var s as string is "Hello, PenguScript!"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.ellipsis with 10), "Hello, ...", "ellipsis"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling ellipsis with "abcdef", 3), "abc", "func"
test "formas funcionales de truncado y prefijos":
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling truncate with "abcdef", 4, ".."), "ab..", "truncate"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling ellipsis with "abcdef", 4), "a...", "ellipsis"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling removeprefix with "abc", "a"), "bc", "removeprefix"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling removesuffix with "abc", "c"), "ab", "removesuffix"

# Parseo
test "parse_int interpreta enteros con espacios y signo":
    var s as string is " 42 "
    var m as maybe int is calling s.parse_int
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (m.is_present), true, "presente"
    if v as int is m:
        calling _expect_eq_int with v, 42, "valor"
test "parse_int rechaza basura y desbordamiento":
    var s as string is "4x"
    var m as maybe int is calling s.parse_int
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (m.is_present), false, "basura"
    var grande as string is "99999999999999999999"
    var g as maybe int is calling grande.parse_int
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (g.is_present), false, "desbordamiento"
test "parse_float calcula el valor decimal":
    var s as string is "3.5"
    var m as maybe float is calling s.parse_float
    if v as float is m:
        calling _expect with (v > 3.4 and v < 3.6), "3.5"
    else:
        calling _expect with false, "3.5 presente"
test "parse_float acepta signo, punto inicial y espacios":
    var a as string is "-0.25"
    var b as string is ".5"
    var c as string is " 2 "
    if va as float is (calling a.parse_float):
        calling _expect with (va > -0.3 and va < -0.2), "-0.25"
    if vb as float is (calling b.parse_float):
        calling _expect with (vb > 0.4 and vb < 0.6), ".5"
    if vc as float is (calling c.parse_float):
        calling _expect with (vc > 1.9 and vc < 2.1), " 2 "
test "parse_float rechaza vacío, basura y exponentes":
    var vacio as string is ""
    var basura as string is "abc"
    var expo as string is "1e3"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with ((calling vacio.parse_float).is_present), false, "vacío"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with ((calling basura.parse_float).is_present), false, "basura"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with ((calling expo.parse_float).is_present), false, "exponente"
test "is_numeric acepta literales exactos":
    var a as string is "-3.5"
    var b as string is ".5"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling a.is_numeric), true, "negativo"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling b.is_numeric), true, "punto inicial"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_numeric with "42"), true, "func"
test "is_numeric rechaza espacios, exponentes y basura":
    var s as string is " 1"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling s.is_numeric), false, "espacio"
    var expo as string is "1e3"
    var doble as string is "1.2.3"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling expo.is_numeric), false, "exponente"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling doble.is_numeric), false, "dos puntos"

# join
test "join une los elementos con el separador":
    var partes as list of string is ["alpha", "beta", "gamma"]
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling join with partes, ", "), "alpha, beta, gamma", "join"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling join with partes, "|"), "alpha|beta|gamma", "otro sep"
test "join de una lista vacía devuelve vacío":
    var partes as list of string is list of string
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling join with partes, ","), "", "vacía"
test "join de un elemento no añade separador":
    var partes as list of string is ["x"]
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling join with partes, ","), "x", "un elemento"
test "join conserva los elementos vacíos":
    var partes as list of string is ["", "x", ""]
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling join with partes, "|"), "|x|", "vacíos"

# Formas funcionales y bordes
test "formas funcionales de longitud y corte":
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling len with "abcd"), 4, "len"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling substring with "abcdef", 1, 3), "bc", "substring"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling char_at with "abc", 1), "b", "char_at"
test "formas funcionales de chars y bytes":
    calling _expect_eq_int with ((calling chars with "ab") length), 2, "chars"
    var letra_a as string is "A"
    var codigos_a as list of int is calling bytes with letra_a
    calling _expect_eq_int with (codigos_a at 0), 65, "bytes"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_empty with ""), true, "is_empty"
test "los métodos no mutan el receptor":
    var s as string is "  hola  "
    var t as string is calling s.trim
    calling _expect_eq_string with s, "  hola  ", "receptor intacto"
    calling _expect_eq_string with t, "hola", "resultado"
test "chars y bytes del string vacío están vacíos":
    var vacio as string is ""
    calling _expect_eq_int with ((calling vacio.chars) length), 0, "chars"
    calling _expect_eq_int with ((calling bytes with vacio) length), 0, "bytes"
test "los predicados de contenido son false con vacío":
    var vacio as string is ""
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling vacio.is_alpha), false, "is_alpha"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling vacio.is_digit), false, "is_digit"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling vacio.is_alnum), false, "is_alnum"
test "formas funcionales de predicados":
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_alpha with "aB"), true, "is_alpha"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_digit with "12"), true, "is_digit"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_alnum with "a1"), true, "is_alnum"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_lower with "a1"), true, "is_lower"
test "to_snake_case separa letras de dígitos":
    var s as string is "a1B"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.to_snake_case), "a1_b", "dígito"
test "parse_int del string vacío devuelve none":
    var vacio as string is ""
    var m as maybe int is calling vacio.parse_int
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (m.is_present), false, "vacío"
test "index_of y last_index_of con sub vacío en vacío":
    var vacio as string is ""
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling vacio.index_of with ""), 0, "index_of"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling vacio.last_index_of with ""), 0, "last_index_of"
test "repeat_join con separador vacío":
    var s as string is "ab"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.repeat_join with 2, ""), "abab", "sin separador"
test "lines con LF final añade una línea vacía":
    var s as string is "a\n"
    var partes as list of string is calling s.lines
    calling _expect_eq_int with (partes length), 2, "dos líneas"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (partes at 1), "", "última vacía"
test "is_numeric rechaza un signo suelto":
    var s as string is "+"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling s.is_numeric), false, "signo solo"
    var cinco as string is "5."
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling cinco.is_numeric), true, "punto final"
test "compare con prefijo común y longitudes distintas":
    var a as string is "abc"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling a.compare with "ab"), 1, "más largo"
    var corto as string is "ab"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling corto.compare with "abc"), -1, "más corto"
test "formas funcionales de reverse y repetición":
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling reverse with "abc"), "cba", "reverse"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling repeat with "ab", 2), "abab", "repeat"
